From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: defcom5-rockchip <286489597+defcom5-rockchip@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: orangepi-5-plus: source vp0 dclk from
 v0pll

The same change the Orange Pi 5/5B carries for HDMI0 4K@120 (FRL modes):
rockchip_rk3588_drm_dclk_set_rate() re-rates the source PLL to the exact
pixel clock only when that PLL is v0pll; gpll/cpll cannot give
1082.89 MHz. Assign dclk_vop0_src to v0pll as the RK3588 EVB boards do.
HDMI1 on vp1 is unchanged.

Proven on an Orange Pi 5 Plus 2026-11-12/13: HDMI0 FRL link training and 4K@120 desktop and playback (Plaid Pi 6.5).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts
@@ -1311,6 +1311,18 @@
     cursor-win-id=<ROCKCHIP_VOP2_ESMART0>;
     rockchip,plane-mask = <(1 << ROCKCHIP_VOP2_CLUSTER0 | 1 << ROCKCHIP_VOP2_ESMART0)>;
     rockchip,primary-plane = <ROCKCHIP_VOP2_CLUSTER0>;
+    /*
+     * HDMI0 4K@120 runs FRL, where dclk cannot be sourced from the HDMI PHY
+     * PLL and comes from the CRU instead. rockchip_rk3588_drm_dclk_set_rate()
+     * only re-rates the source PLL to the exact pixel clock when that PLL is
+     * v0pll (gpll/cpll are shared and only offer integer dividers), so hang
+     * dclk_vop0_src off v0pll, as the Orange Pi 5/5B change does. v0pll is
+     * shared with vp2 (DP, rk3588s.dtsi), so a simultaneous DP output would
+     * contend for its rate. HDMI1 (vp1) keeps its PHY-sourced dclk: only one
+     * port can run FRL from v0pll.
+     */
+    assigned-clocks = <&cru DCLK_VOP0_SRC>;
+    assigned-clock-parents = <&cru PLL_V0PLL>;
 };
 
 &vp1 {
